Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Quantum Machine Learning in Phase Space", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A quantum circuit is a tensor network, and a tensor network contraction is \
a sequence of array products - the computation a neural net performs. The \
framework closes that loop: a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumCircuitOperator"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumCircuitOperator", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f76f11bc-e81c-4492-b21c-b6a44a8826c1"],
 " compiles to a tensor network, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`", "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",
  ExpressionUUID->"4db67d99-2357-48d5-9e7c-d66f50e963f5"],
 " contracts that network into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetGraph"]], "paclet:ref/NetGraph"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7902c450-b71c-4fdb-8d16-774b0d8d647e"],
 " rather than an array, with every circuit tensor held in a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetArrayLayer"]], "paclet:ref/NetArrayLayer"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1256c4ec-96a4-4da6-9488-4afe7719048d"],
 ". The circuit becomes the model. Nothing about the forward computation is \
assembled by hand; the only layer added here is the loss."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"540922a5-d44a-4d50-96d6-9cb2ecb72dee"],

Cell["\<\
The net framework computes over real numbers, and that is not an obstacle: in \
the phase-space picture a state is a Wigner quasi-probability vector and \
every circuit tensor is real, so the whole pipeline stays inside what a net \
can represent. This tutorial compiles a circuit to a net, differentiates \
through it, and trains a gate until gradient descent recovers a rotation \
angle.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e9600055-0293-47ea-9be5-7def109267c0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<<", " ", "Wolfram`QuantumFramework`"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b8ca290b-cd76-4b47-8c8d-2b985ed78f27"],

Cell["A Circuit Is the Model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f8ced7d3-2396-4467-8fdb-ec073c325464"],

Cell["\<\
A circuit can carry its own initial state, so the whole computation - \
prepare, then rotate - is one object:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"61ff1638-aaee-421e-8806-cbf779e5f6f7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qc", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", "0.7", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"92fa1dfc-52b7-4757-8235-fc52bee98673"],

